      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ \\mathrm{SD}(z_{O}) $ is the observed phenotypic standard deviation in the random-mating population. Sampling distributions of means are usually approximately normally distributed, so t may be treated as t-distributed with L-1 degrees of freedom.",
